---
import Layout from '@layouts/default.astro';
import profileImage from '@assets/images/profile.webp';
---

<Layout title="About">
  <div class="max-width-56 width-100 margin-auto column flex gap-2">
    <span></span>
    <section class="gap grid justify-content-center text-align-center">
      <img
        src={profileImage.src}
        alt="Andrew Noblet profile photo"
        class="profile-image margin-auto"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <h1>Meet Andrew Noblet</h1>
      <p class="bold-5 max-width-56">
        Hello! I'm <strong>Andrew Noblet</strong>, a software engineer with a
        truly global perspective—born in Chile and shaped by experiences living
        in Puerto Rico, Ohio, and now New York. I'm passionate about creating
        fast, accessible, and beautifully simple web experiences that truly
        serve users. Drawing wisdom from Eastern philosophy (Confucianism,
        Buddhism, Shintoism) and the rich narratives of Greek mythology, I
        believe technology should empower everyone through elegant, minimal
        design that respects both human nature and digital possibility.
      </p>
    </section>
    <card-component>
      <ul class="column flex gap-0-5 font-size-1-125">
        <li><strong>Full Name:</strong> Andrew Noblet</li>
        <li><strong>Born in:</strong> Chile</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Global Experience:</strong> Chile, Puerto Rico, Ohio, and now <strong
            >New York</strong
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub:</strong>
          <a href="https://github.com/anoblet" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >anoblet</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Interests:</strong> Skateboarding, snowboarding, guitar, 3D printing,
          smart home technology, bike riding, politics, history, Eastern philosophy
          (Confucianism, Buddhism, Shintoism), and Greek mythology
        </li>
      </ul>
    </card-component>

    <card-component>
      <h2 class="font-size-1-25 margin-bottom-0-5">Philosophy & Approach</h2>
      <ul class="column flex gap-0-5 font-size-1-125">
        <li>
          <strong>Eastern Wisdom:</strong> Drawing from Confucian balance, Buddhist
          mindfulness, and Shinto harmony to create technology that respects both
          human nature and digital possibility.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Minimalism:</strong> Less is more—simple, elegant solutions that
          do exactly what they need to do, inspired by the principle of restraint.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Composability:</strong> Building reusable, modular components that
          work beautifully together, like stories from Greek mythology that weave
          universal truths.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Continuous Learning:</strong> Embracing growth and new perspectives,
          inspired by the Confucian ideal of lifelong cultivation and wisdom.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Favorite Tools:</strong> Astro and Lit for their simplicity, performance,
          and developer experience—tools that embody the minimalist philosophy.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </card-component>

    <card-component>
      <h2 class="font-size-1-25 margin-bottom-0-5">Technical Values</h2>
      <ul class="column flex gap-0-5 font-size-1-125">
        <li>
          <strong>Open Source & Linux:</strong> Passionate advocate for open-source
          software and Linux systems—believing in transparency, community collaboration,
          and the power of shared knowledge.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Performance First:</strong> Every millisecond matters. Optimizing
          bundle sizes, leveraging efficient loading strategies, and respecting users'
          time and bandwidth.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Atomic CSS:</strong> Utility-first styling that promotes consistency,
          maintainability, and composability across all components and pages.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Accessibility by Design:</strong> Creating inclusive experiences
          that work for everyone, regardless of ability, device, or context.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Minimal Dependencies:</strong> Favoring lean, purposeful toolchains
          like pnpm, Prettier, and Husky that enhance workflow without bloat.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </card-component>

    <card-component>
      <h2 class="font-size-1-25 margin-bottom-0-5">
        Early Programming Journey
      </h2>
      <p class="margin-bottom-0-5">
        My passion for programming started early. At <strong>age 14</strong>, I
        read a thick programming book cover-to-cover, diving deep into the
        fundamentals that would shape my approach to software development.
      </p>

      <p>
        By <strong>age 15</strong>, I was building my own water-cooled computer
        to get the power I needed for gaming. Let's just say I learned the
        importance of planning the hard way—I definitely needed those towels to
        mop up my mistakes! 😅
      </p>
    </card-component>

    <consultation-component class="margin-top-4"></consultation-component>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .profile-image {
    border-radius: 50%;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--tertiary-color);
    display: block;
    height: 50vw;
    max-height: 16rem;
    max-width: 16rem;
    object-fit: cover;
    position: relative;
    width: 50vw;
    z-index: 1;
  }
</style>
<script>
  import '@components/card';
  import '@components/consultation';
</script>
